WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
Hold a ruler at its middle
and rock it back and forth.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.270
It turns easily.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.690
Now hold the same ruler at
one end and do the same.

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.030
Same mass, same length, same twist.

5
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.170
Yet it is four times as hard to spin up.

6
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.290
Not twice.

7
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.780
Four times.

8
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.080
Where does that four come from?

9
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.620
In this mission, you'll slice
a solid into tiny pieces,

10
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.340
and add up every piece with an integral.

11
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.200
Then you'll do it for
rings and solid wheels,

12
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.680
and for a rod whose mass
piles up at one end.

13
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:37.550
Your mission: show why spinning the ruler
about one end makes it four times as

14
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.840
hard to spin up.
